    <forecast>
        <area aac="SA_FA001" description="South Australia" type="region">
            <forecast-period start-time-local="2026-08-13T21:19:36+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-13T21:19:36+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-13T11:49:36Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-13T11:49:36Z">
                <text type="warning_summary_footer">For latest warnings go to www.bom.gov.au, subscribe to RSS feeds, call 1300 659 210* or listen for warnings on relevant TV and radio broadcasts.</text>
                <text type="synoptic_situation">A high pressure system centred over SA will remain near stationary into Friday before drifting to the southeast to be located west of Tasmania on Saturday, with a ridge expected to remain over South Australia. A trough over QLD pushes into the far northeast of SA from later Saturday through to later Monday.</text>
                <text type="product_footer">* Calls to 1300 numbers cost around 27.5c incl. GST, higher from mobiles or public phones.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
        <area aac="SA_PW013" description="North West Pastoral" type="public-district" parent-aac="SA_FA001">
            <forecast-period index="0" start-time-local="2026-08-13T21:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-14T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-13T11:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-13T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. Light winds.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="1" start-time-local="2026-08-14T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-13T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Coober Pedy. Slight chance of a shower in the far west at night. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. Light winds becoming east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h in the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 4 and 7 with daytime temperatures reaching between 18 and 21.</text>
                <text type="uv_alert">Sun protection 10:00am to 3:00pm, UV Index predicted to reach 5 [Moderate]</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="2" start-time-local="2026-08-15T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-14T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Medium chance of showers west of Coober Pedy, near zero chance elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm north of Marla. Winds easterly 15 to 25 km/h becoming light in the evening. Overnight temperatures falling to around 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 15 and 19.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="3" start-time-local="2026-08-16T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-15T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Cloudy. Slight chance of a shower. Light winds becoming east to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h during the morning. Overnight temperatures falling to between 6 and 9 with daytime temperatures reaching between 17 and 20.</text>
            </forecast-period>
            <forecast-period index="4" start-time-local="2026-08-17T00:00:00+09:30" end-time-local="2026-08-18T00:00:00+09:30" start-time-utc="2026-08-16T14:30:00Z" end-time-utc="2026-08-17T14:30:00Z">
                <text type="forecast">Partly cloudy. The chance of morning fog south of Woomera. Slight chance of a shower south of Woomera, most likely in the afternoon. Near zero chance of rain elsewhere. The chance of a thunderstorm east of Stuart Highway in the afternoon. Winds northeast to southeasterly 15 to 25 km/h tending north to northeasterly during the day then tending east to northeasterly during the afternoon. Overnight temperatures falling to between 5 and 8 with daytime temperatures reaching between 19 and 23.</text>
            </forecast-period>
        </area>
